\ Exercise the strict-AOT compound-fallback build error: in
\ --interpreter-fallback=false mode, a compiled caller that dispatches
\ to an uncompiled compound callee must fail the build with a diagnostic
\ that names the caller, the callee, the line, and the callee's
\ NotCompilableReason. `bi` carries row-variable parameter effects, so
\ its body still fails to compile (NC.13). Calling it from compiled
\ code must surface as a build error rather than a runtime fallback.
1 [ 2 + ] [ 3 + ] bi . .
